{{Card Infobox|Cost=3|Rarity=Rare|Type=Troop|Arena=Barbarian Bowl|ReleaseDate=19 September 2016}}
{{SubpageNavBox|Hero=yes}}{{Quote|Flying, armored and powerful. What could be its weakness?! Cupcakes.}}

The Mega Minion is a {{Rarity|Rare}} [[Cards|card]] that is unlocked from the [[Arenas|Barbarian Bowl (Arena 3)]]. It spawns a single-target, air-targeting, melee, air [[:Category:Troop Cards|troop]] with moderate hitpoints and high damage. It appears as an enlarged [[Minions|Minion]] wearing a set of armor with a mask, chainmail, and a team-colored belt. A Mega Minion card costs 3 [[Elixir]] to deploy.

==Strategy==
{{Battle Deck with Card|:Category:Battle Decks using the Mega Minion Card}}
*Unlike the [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Lumberjack]], and [[Prince]], the Mega Minion is vulnerable on offense alone if you were to counterpush after trading some. The Mega Minion, however, excels at defense and should be mostly used as a defensive [[Cards|card]] as it has a high damage output but is slower than [[Minions]]. However, it is often used on the offensive as a support card, being able to clear out low-medium hitpoint units and deal significant damage to everything else.
*Its high damage to moderate hitpoints allow it to be able to defend relatively well against many ground-based pushes. Its defensive value is even greater since it is much more resistant to [[:Category:Spell Cards|spells]], unlike the [[Minion Horde]] and [[Minions]]. However, it can't deal with swarms very effectively due to its slow hit speed.
**Also, unlike the Minions, it can counter area damage units such as the [[Witch]], [[Wizard]], [[Baby Dragon]], [[Skeleton Dragons]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Princess|Princess,]] [[Firecracker]], [[Ice Wizard]], and [[Executioner]] without being destroyed. However, it doesn't fare so well against [[Inferno Dragon]] due to the damage ramp up and the Mega Minion's relatively low health.
*Against ranged troops that can target air troops like the [[Musketeer]], [[Electro Dragon]], [[Mother Witch]], [[Flying Machine]], [[Archer Queen]], and [[Electro Wizard]], place the Mega Minion on top of them, to negate their range advantage and defeat them. This will save more of its hitpoints in case the player wants to use a tank in front of it for a counterattack.
*If ignored, the Mega Minion will be able to reach the Crown Tower and attack once if the player is using the [[Tower Princess]] or [[Cannoneer]], dealing a fair amount of chip damage. However, a [[Zap]] or a [[Giant Snowball]] will allow the Crown Tower to defeat it for a positive Elixir trade. If the player is using the [[Dagger Duchess]], she will kill it quick enough, causing it to get no damage on the Crown Tower. For this reason, if you know you're going to play against a Mega Minion, it may be a good idea to use the Dagger Duchess as your tower troop.
*The Mega Minion is a very effective counter against the [[Balloon]] for a cheap cost. Its moderate hitpoints allow it to survive spells from [[Zap]] to [[Poison]] while its damage allows it to quickly deal with the [[Balloon]] itself. Place the Mega Minion on the Balloon's path to further lower its chances of connecting to the Tower.
*The Mega Minion pairs well with the [[Lava Hound]] since it deals with any moderate-health defending units trying to destroy the Lava Hound while the [[Lava Hound]] tanks most of the incoming damage. When the Lava Hound bursts, the Mega Minion's moderate health will allow it to tank [[:Category:Crown Towers|Crown Tower]] hits while the Lava Pups deal massive damage to the Tower. Naturally, the Mega Minion also fits in very well with the Double Dragon strategy, as its high damage allows it to quickly deal with major threats such as a [[Musketeer]] or [[Wizard]], something that the Baby Dragon and Inferno Dragon both fail at.
**On the other hand, it is a great counter to an opposing Lava Hound. Its high damage will quickly defeat the Lava Hound itself, and it is also high enough to OHKO each Lava Pup.
*Cheap air-targeting troops like the [[Archers]], [[Dart Goblin]], Firecracker, and [[Spear Goblins]] are great counters to the Mega Minion. Place them far enough from it to ensure that none of the troops are OHKOed by the Mega Minion, to ensure a more potent counterattack.
*If placed optimally, any troop, even [[Skeletons]] or [[Bats]], can distract the Mega Minion long enough for any [[:Category:Tower Troop Cards|tower troop]] to defeat it. Any spawner [[:Category:Building Cards|building]] can also work in a similar way.
*The Mega Minion pairs well with the [[Miner]]. The Mega Minion can be utilized defensively first and then after going for a counterattack, the [[Miner]] can be deployed to distract the Crown Tower. However, the Mega Minion is notably slower than other similar troops, so try to place the Miner further back to prevent the opponent's defending troops to distract the Mega Minion when it arrives.
*To defend against a [[Minion Horde]], the player can place this card in the middle of the Arena so that the Minion Horde will be pulled to the center, increasing the length of their way to the Crown Tower and distracting them. The Mega Minion will take out 2 or 3 Minions while your Crown Tower continually attacks. However, it is likely that you will still suffer some damage so it is best to use splash damage troops or spells.
*When placed and timed correctly, a Mega Minion combined with [[Skeletons]] can fully counter a [[Little Prince]] and Guardienne for a +2 Elixir trade. Likewise, this duo works against most ground troops.
*If the player can predict a [[Princess]] placed at the bridge, they can place the Mega Minion to counter her for a neutral Elixir trade. This tactic also works against a [[Princess]] walking towards the bridge, and is more effective compared to other cheap cards due to the Mega Minion's higher hitpoints.
*The [[Void]] is the only spell effective against a Mega Minion. It will be able to destroy it in just 2 hits for a neutral Elixir trade. The player can deploy any troop inside the Void's radius to allow the Mega Minion to completely survive the spell.
*The [[Phoenix]] can be used as a replacement for the Mega Minion. It offers higher hitpoints, a faster attack speed, some additional death damage, the ability to respawn after being defeated, and is resistant to the [[Monk]]'s ability. In exchange, the Mega Minion is cheaper by 1 Elixir, and has significantly higher damage.
