==Trivia == 
*The design of the Mega Minion resembles [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gargoyle_(monster) gargoyles]. The gargoyle is a fantasy and horror monster inspired by the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gargoyle gargoyle architectural element]. While they were believed in mythology to frighten away evil spirits, the idea of such statues physically coming to life is a more recent notion. They are usually made of magically animated or transformed stone, but have animal or chimera traits and are often guardians of a place such as a cathedral or castle. They can also be depicted as vessels for demonic possession or as a living species resembling statues.
**In the French and Japanese language settings of the game, the Mega Minion's name translates to "Mega Gargoyle". In the Arabic, Chinese, Malaysian, Thai, and Vietnamese language settings of the game, the Mega Minion's name translates to "Giant Minion", "Armored Undead", "Big Minion", "Armored Drone", and "Super Minion" respectively.
*The Mega Minion was the first [[Cards|card]] to be introduced in the game along with a Special Offer in the [[Shop]].
*The Mega Minion, along with the [[Minions]], [[Bomber]], [[Skeletons]], [[Skeleton Dragons]], [[Ice Spirit]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Ice Golem]], [[Dart Goblin]], [[Elixir Golem]], [[Goblin Cage|Goblin Brawler]], [[Guards]], [[Baby Dragon]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Golem]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Executioner]], [[Mega Knight]], [[Inferno Dragon]], [[Royal Ghost]], and [[Lava Hound]], are featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Monsters monster] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
*When deployed, the Mega Minion says "''Cupcake''". However, the Mega Minion's audio is muffled.
**The Mega Minion is 1 of 24 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] that speak distinct words when on the field, the others being Mini P.E.K.K.A., [[Wizard]], [[Hog Rider]], P.E.K.K.A., [[Dark Prince]], Bowler, [[Ram Rider]], [[Electro Wizard]], [[Princess]], [[Ice Wizard]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Lumberjack]], [[Mother Witch]], [[Fisherman]], [[Goblin Machine]], [[Super Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Santa Hog Rider]], [[Super Magic Archer]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Boss Bandit]], [[Archer Queen]], [[Little Prince]], and the [[Terry]].
*When the Mega Minion is defeated, its helmet falls to the ground. The other units that drop items upon death are the [[Knight]], [[Rascals|Rascal Boy]], Dark Prince, Executioner, [[Mega Knight]], [[Sparky]], [[Fisherman]], [[Super Knight]], Golden Knight, and the Little Prince.
*The Mega Minion is 1 of 10 cards to have an alliterative name, the others being the [[Royal Recruits]], [[Goblin Gang]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Barbarian Barrel]], Ram Rider, [[Dagger Duchess]], [[Boss Bandit]], and the [[Mighty Miner]].
*The Minions and [[Minion Horde]]'s descriptions say that the regular Minions are "unarmored", which hinted the addition of the "armored" Mega Minion.
**According to a Clash-A-Rama comic [https://clasharama.fandom.com/wiki/Clash-A-Rama!_Comic_Strips?file=BRING-YOUR-CHILD-TO-WORK-DAY_Final.jpg strip], a Minion is the Mega Minion's child.
*The Mega Minion's health is a little higher than 3 Minions of equivalent level put together, while its damage is slightly lower.
*The grill covering the Mega Minion's mouth is very similar to the visor on the [[Prince]]'s helmet.
*The Mega Minion's gender has been confirmed as male, as the [https://make.supercell.com/en/campaign/3468 Mega Minion Emote Supercell Make campaign] referred to Mega Minion as "he".
*The Mega Minion is the subject of an [[Emotes|Emote]].
**The Mega Minion Mute Emote was created by [https://make.supercell.com/en/creation/i-can-not-hear-you LordFink] on [[Supercell Make]].
*Its range was shown as 2 before the [[Version History#July%202019%20Update%20(1/7/2019)|July 2019 Update]].
*The Mega Minion was featured in the winning [[Battle Decks|decks]] of multiple Clash Royale Tournaments. More specifically:
**The Mega Minion was featured in the winning deck of the [https://youtu.be/LWQjS0e6iiE Super Magical Cup Tournament], by a player called CMcHugh.
**The Mega Minion was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/1fuCnNBTqBU?feature=share King's Cup Tournament], by a player called TMD YAOYAO.
**The Mega Minion was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kIGdeKaT_is The Crown Duel Tournament], by a player called Backstabx.
*The initial balance change for Mega Minion on the [[Version History#Balance%20Changes%20(4/4/2023)|4/4/2023 balance changes]] was an attack time interval decrease to 1.3 seconds (from 1.6 seconds), but it was raised to 1.5 seconds [https://royaleapi.com/blog/season-46-balance-wip last minute].

